Interpretation
  The m=4 spike remains isolated in the targeted family through m=120.
  After m=24, the best row found is far below 1/3 and also far below the
  B30 non-family new-speed competitors.  This does not prove HYP-2671,
  but it reinforces the idea that m=4 is a finite resonance to isolate,
  not the first term of a high-ratio tail.
